{
  // Seasonal perks - BSG "Seasonal Character" mechanic (EFT patch 1.1.0.0).
  //
  // NOT SERVED BY TARKOV.DEV. tarkov.dev does serve the pvp-season game mode
  // (json.tarkov.dev/pvp-season/*), but it has no seasonal-perks endpoint and no
  // perk type, so seasonal perks are absent upstream. They ship here as an
  // overlay addition keyed by the perk id, mirroring how editions.json5 carries
  // data tarkov.dev omits.
  //
  // Source: verified in-game (Seasonal Character perk selection screen).
  // Proof: EFT patch 1.1.0.0 notes (Seasonal Character), 2026-08-03.
  //   https://steamdb.info/patchnotes/24536010/
  // Verified in-game: 2026-08-03.
  //
  // Fields: id, type (tier: common|personal), name, description, points
  // (perk-point value shown on the selection screen; null = none),
  // mutuallyExclusiveSeasonalPerkIds, and effects[] (the raw in-game effect
  // values as the game stores them; each effect has an effectId plus its values).
  //
  // description vs effects: `description` is the verbatim in-game display text;
  // `effects[]` are the raw values the game actually applies. Where the two
  // disagree - e.g. Handyman's text says crafting time "-50%" while
  // craft_time_multiplicator is 0.87, Polydipsia's text says "15% faster" while
  // hydration_drain_multiplicator is 1.2 (20%), and Average's text and
  // skill_level_preset exclude Crafting while its skill_not_growing list still
  // includes it - the mismatch is faithful to how the game itself presents the
  // perk: BSG's display strings and underlying values are not always consistent.
  // Both sides are captured as-is; do NOT "reconcile" them to make them agree.
  //
  // effects[].itemFilter matches tarkov.dev's served ItemFilters shape:
  // allowedCategories / allowedItems / excludedCategories / excludedItems, each
  // an array of tarkov.dev ids (item template ids for items, item-category node
  // ids for categories). Ids only - names resolve through tarkov.dev's locale
  // system, exactly as tarkov.dev serves item slot/grid filters.

  // ===========================================================================
